-- A REFUSE message is a LITERAL, not an expression: the grammar admits only a
-- literal in that position, so a computed message is a PARSE error rather than
-- a type error.
--
-- That is deliberate. A refusal's reason has to be readable without running the
-- program (so it can be reported and, later, analysed per reason), and keeping
-- the payload a literal is also what lets the evaluation machine raise a
-- refusal with no new stack frame.

GIVETH A NUMBER
`bad refusal` MEANS REFUSE (1 PLUS 1)
